M28_field_idata         58/58   *** PREDICTED CLEAN SWEEP, and this one is a FLOOR question.
                                D6 phase 4 stores 0x100000 at MASK0; phase 5 then writes
                                0x100100000, and under the mutant f = idata >> 20 = 0x1001 is
                                rejected -- so the arm DECLINES and KEEPS THE PREVIOUS VALUE,
                                which is 0x100000, which is exactly what `wmask0 hif' wants.
                                The row is vacuous against its own named mutant BECAUSE OF PHASE
                                ORDER, not because of the value it drives.
