Commit:     indigoidk <indigoidk@users.noreply.github.com>
CommitDate: Wed Sep 9 23:17:38 2026 -0500

    #516 lcairqstubkill: every ISA interrupt on alphabook1 routed into a function whose whole body was fatal()+exit(1)
    
    dev_lca.c registered lca_interrupt_assert/_deassert as bare kills -- no guard, no inspection
    of the argument -- and DEVINIT(lca) hands that path to bus_isa_init, so a store of 0xAA to
    the 8042 command port (four guest instructions, the standard self-test) ended the host.
    Witnessed at rung 3 before any edit (lca_irqstub_probe.py 3/6; lca_irqstub_uart_probe.py 2/5).
    
    FIX: option-set member 3 at BOTH stubs -- decline plus a bounded, PER-INSTANCE latched
    announce naming Alpha's missing delivery, one latch bit per stub so the two are
    distinguishable.  Stated narrowly: the host stops dying; interrupts do not start working,
    because cpu_dyntrans.c delivers for five architectures and has no Alpha arm, and
    cd.alpha.irq_asserted is written and never read.  IMPLEMENT is filed as alphaintdeliver so
    the missing subsystem is tracked rather than buried.  FAULT (member 5) was unavailable:
    memory_rw.c dispatches an exception only for MIPS and M88K.  STOP-GUEST, a member the design
    packet omitted, is recorded and rejected: the stub fires on ordinary ISA interrupts, so
    halting makes alphabook1 unbootable.
    
    DETECTOR, rebuilt three times under the vacuity floor:
      6 rows   -> blind at the deassert site: a verbatim exit(1) reinstated there scored 6/6,
                  as did the deassert announce disabled and the two latch bits collapsed
                  (killtable_opus_20260909/*_shipped.raw).  The round had disclosed that site
                  under clause (e); both Anthropic seats overturned it -- the edge needs ONE
                  guest load, verified in dev_pckbc.c by reading.
      11 rows  -> the measuring seat's instrument, adopted as measured: drains the 0x55 reply
                  into the dead LPT pointer so a second cycle costs nothing.  The main loop's
                  own staged patch would have turned `irq honest' into a disjunction over both
                  sites (both announces contain "Alpha has no") -- measured 8/8 by the seat
                  in its own first attempt, and discarded unapplied.
      12 rows  -> the pass-2 panel's own mutant (assert-guard latch-bit swap, minimax) swept
                  11/11.  Reachability referred to the measuring seat with the author's
                  interest disclosed; it MEASURED a second synchronous ISA line (ns16550 on
                  IRQ 4, inline dev_ns16550_tick, unconditional) with an edge trace.  L2, in
                  round: raise and drop the UART between the 8042's assert and its drain.
    
    TABLES G + H, one instrument (frozen copies byte-identical), baseline named and cmp'd,
    scratch clone, restore verified against SEC + rebuild:
      base 12/12; 2 sites x 8 edits = 16 cells, 14 killed, 2 measured equivalent with their
      derivations (`|=' -> `=' on the assert arm: the stub is entered only on edges of the
      AGGREGATE, which is 0 until the first assert, and old_isa_assert is recomputed at every
      entry; `d != NULL' removed: dev_lca.c:498-500 is the only registration).  The two
      assignment-bit-swap cells were built last, after pass 3 found them unswept (M14 8/12,
      M15 11/12).  The chain closes on pass 3: zero floor breaches with a complete, measured
      denominator; the only material changed afterwards is contract text.
    
    Three defective repairs preceded the clean one, all the incomplete-edit shape (a correction
    appended below a stale line; a label corrected into a different falsehood; a readback phase
    added to the program list and not the command list, so the BASELINE failed 11/12).  Two
    apparatus defects of the main loop recorded rather than dropped: driver columns that could
    not fail, and a panel read from a stale shadow _scratchpad.
    
    Propagated to est/ and all three build trees; two-part clearance RUN, CLEAN/FRESH on every
    row (_scratchpad/propagate516.out).  Nine seat answers from the two 2026-09-08 panels were
    on disk and recorded nowhere until today; all recorded.  Four panels + two Agent seats +
    codex readings recorded by name; agy deliberately not fired (measurement reserve).
    
    Also in this commit: the unread-review harvest and the day's adjudication docket
    (tools/pipeline/ledger.json -- 18 rulings across 10 rows, 7 new rows filed), because the
    ledger is one file; codex_answer.py's refusal detector re-keyed on POSITION; the
    check_probe_wiring.py MANIFEST note for lca_irqstub_probe.py updated from "post-fix green
    PENDING" to measured, with its detector-shaped-but-CLASS_WITNESS state filed; a dated pointer at
    CHANGELOG.md's older "still open, filed" list (pcc2c040kill / pcc2defaultkill, both since fixed) so a
    grep for the subject lands on the correction; eight OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md entries for rows filed
    today; the #515 pass-2 receipt the gate found missing; and seventeen CLASS_RESEARCH entries in
    check_probe_wiring.py's MANIFEST for the instruments and mutators preserved beside the kill tables --
    the pre-commit gate refused the first attempt because they had no class (the earlier green run
    predated staging them), and each entry is written from the file's own header.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

