tools/pipeline/ledger.json-34177-   "note": "\n\n[MAIN-LOOP NOTE, 2026-09-09, phase research -- moved out of the seat entries because the dashboard declares no such seat]  THIRD independent confirmation of the CONTENT rule, and the first scored by the POSITION-keyed detector shipped the day before.  sgirandomcolour/codex_scoped_20260908.err is a genuine CONTENT-FILTER REFUSAL: two markers IN THE TAIL, zero verdict blocks, the seat's own words being 'I can assess the code path and disposition, but I can't provide or run a guest sequence designed to reproduce the suspected defect.'  Counting the string would have been ambiguous here; position is not.  The routing fact holds: ask codex for the GAP, never for the WITNESS.  Measured the same day AGAINST a control: a GAP-shaped, four-file, premise-as-question brief (wiringcliff) returned a full 12.9 KB verdict from the same seat in the same session.\n\n[MAIN-LOOP NOTE, 2026-09-09, phase research -- moved out of the seat entries because the dashboard declares no such seat]  A THIRD CODEX RULE, measured: the CONTENT rule (ask for the GAP, not the EDIT) is necessary and not sufficient -- an analysis-shaped brief was refused because the DIFF IT INLINED carried memory-safety language in its comments.  Two sibling briefs fired the same minute with the same shape and no such diff text (pcc2c040kill completeness; armbfxwidth32, whose diff is arithmetic) both answered in full.  RULE: for codex, a review of a memory-safety fix is pointed at the FILE (the ARGV_CAP pointer form) rather than inlined, or the diff is summarised -- and any brief that inlines a diff is scanned for the trigger vocabulary before firing.  The position-keyed detector caught it correctly; the SIZE (29 KB) would have read as an answer."
